      "problem": "What is the cardinality of $B\\times A$ for $B={1,2,3,...,100}$ and $A={a}?$",
      "worked_solution": "For any two finite sets $B$ and $A,$ the cardinality of $B\\times A$ is\n\n$$\n|B\\times A|=|B|\\cdot |A|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|B\\times A| & =|B|\\cdot |A| \\\\  & =100\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
